CLOUD/DEVOPS DAY 05 — S3 SECURITY MISCONFIGURATIONS
Commands Reference Sheet
==========================================

--- BUCKET BASICS ---
awslocal s3 mb s3://<bucket-name>
awslocal s3 cp <file> s3://<bucket-name>/
awslocal s3 ls s3://<bucket-name>/

--- BUCKET POLICY (the misconfiguration lives here) ---
awslocal s3api put-bucket-policy --bucket <bucket-name> --policy file://policy.json
awslocal s3api get-bucket-policy --bucket <bucket-name>
awslocal s3api delete-bucket-policy --bucket <bucket-name>

--- THE DANGEROUS PATTERN TO RECOGNIZE ---
"Principal": "*"            # anyone, no authentication required
"Action": "s3:GetObject"    # read access to objects
"Resource": "<bucket>/*"    # applies to every object in the bucket
# all three together = anyone on the internet can read every file in the bucket

--- TESTING "AS AN ATTACKER" (no AWS credentials at all) ---
curl http://localhost:4566/<bucket-name>/<object-key>
curl -i http://localhost:4566/<bucket-name>/<object-key>   # -i shows the HTTP status code too

--- REAL AWS: BLOCK PUBLIC ACCESS (account/bucket-level safety net) ---
# aws s3api put-public-access-block --bucket <bucket-name> --public-access-block-configuration \
#   BlockPublicAcls=true,IgnorePublicAcls=true,BlockPublicPolicy=true,RestrictPublicBuckets=true
# (this setting exists on real AWS as an extra safety net, separate from bucket policies)

--- CHECKING FOR THIS MISCONFIGURATION (the auditor's angle) ---
awslocal s3api get-bucket-policy --bucket <bucket-name> 2>&1 | grep -i '"Principal": "\*"'
awslocal s3api get-bucket-policy-status --bucket <bucket-name>   # real AWS: tells you if a bucket IS public

